WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.460
Few franchises have a concept as evocative
as The Purge.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:09.310
The allegory-heavy property puts forth the
premise of an annual 12-hour period in which

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:14.540
all crime in the US is legal, an idea introduced
with the series' first movie in 2013.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:19.679
The fourth movie, The First Purge, takes audiences
back to the first experimental instance of

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.840
what would later become a violent tradition.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.300
Set in the New York City borough of Staten
Island, the horror-thriller hybrid provides

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.400
the clearest look yet at the beginnings of
the Purge as a national institution.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.330
If you're not sure that you picked up on everything
the movie was putting down, stay with us as

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:38.360
we break down the ending and thematic takeaways
of The First Purge.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.620
Defend the neighborhood

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.359
Act three of The First Purge turns into a
full-on action movie as drug kingpin Dmitri

00:00:46.359 --> 00:00:50.260
storms the towers of the Park Hill housing
projects to protect his friends on the fourteenth

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:50.760
floor.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.140
By this point, the movie has officially turned
from a citizen-on-citizen free-for-all into

00:00:55.149 --> 00:00:59.829
a government-sanctioned extermination campaign,
as the international militia hired by the

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:02.760
NFFA begins clearing the building floor-by-floor.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:07.200
It's dramatic irony that the only defender
of the vulnerable people in the housing project

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.470
is the friendly neighborhood narcotics salesman,
who apparently happens to spend every moment

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:15.860
away from his business lifting weights, eating
protein, and getting insanely good at using

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.520
firearms.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:21.160
Far from the typical media portrayal of a
drug dealer, Dmitri is a homegrown Batman

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:24.880
figure, his neighborhood's wealthy, well-equipped,
most capable defender.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:28.780
Unlike the hyper right-wing government and
ruling class that is literally trying to kill

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:33.750
the neighborhood, this businessman-turned-warrior
is an authority figure who values his community

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.820
and keeping people safe.

00:01:35.149 --> 00:01:38.979
He's not your typical protagonist, and it's
one of the things that makes this particular

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.780
Purge installment so intriguing.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.120
Intentional extermination

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.100
After two acts' worth of tension in the streets,
the government takes the gloves off for the

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.220
movie's brutal finale.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:53.680
At this point, the undercurrent of class warfare
and exploitation that's informed the whole

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:58.909
series is revealed in all of its ugliness,
as the Purge is identified as a tool for exterminating

00:01:58.909 --> 00:01:59.880
the lower class.

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:05.119
The event isn't a solution to society's problems,
but a scapegoating of society's weakest, with

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:08.420
free passes going to the forces in control
that are actually to blame.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.530
In a country where the economic divide between
the upper and lower classes has never been

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:15.180
more dramatic, this is a message that resonates.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.820
In our very real world, the poor are often
blamed for their own circumstances, instead

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.220
of the predatory forces that exploit them
and keep them down.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:27.720
In the just-slightly-heightened world of The
Purge, they're not just blamed for their own

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.280
poverty; they're intentionally exterminated.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.280
The NFFA isn't just relying on its private

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.880
militia to exterminate the poor.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:41.640
In order to make sure that the experimental
first Purge actually pops off, the government

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.920
injects a massive influx of heavy weaponry
into the Staten Island black market.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.900
Most of these weapons are handily requisitioned
by Dmitri's staff, who use the arsenal for

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:54.500
their own counteroffensive against the government-sponsored
invaders.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:58.740
This plot turn speaks to a number of tactics
that have been used, allegedly or not, by

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.820
the US government.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:05.000
As The First Purge establishes, the NFFA believes
that death needs to happen on a massive scale

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:09.300
during the experiment in order to create the
political capital for a national Purge.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:13.980
To achieve that end, they're willing to covertly
arm the population with heavy artillery.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.370
It's a fact that the US government sends weapons
all over the place to aid with causes, nations,

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:23.080
and groups that it supports around the world,
directly fueling conflicts for its own benefit.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:27.600
In The First Purge, the government sends out
arms to exterminate its own people - another

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.520
instance of the movie taking something real,
and adding a sinister twist.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.640
The First Purge clearly wraps the government

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:41.239
and its allies in recognizable symbols of
white supremacy, taking the racist undercurrent

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.580
that's always been associated with the Purge
and making it explicit.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:50.120
It's not just a class war the NFFA is gunning
for - it's a race war with a Nazi-esque mission.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:54.610
It's no accident that the fourth Purge movie
features a cast, according to producer James

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:59.319
DeMonaco, that's 90% black, because the theme
of white violence against black communities

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.720
is at the heart of what the movie's trying
to convey.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.080
The movie plays with potent iconography.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:08.460
To help spread violence on Staten Island,
the government lets in goons with red, white,

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:12.620
and blue KKK hoods, evoking decades of history
of racist violence.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:17.290
Blue-eyed, blond-haired, government-sanctioned
militia men wear blackface masks, or dress

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:20.590
like SS officers as they attack the Staten
Island community.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:25.040
Acts of violence in the movie uncomfortably
evoke real life hate crimes, with attackers

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.640
bearing torches and wearing crosses that clearly
evoke recognizable hate symbols.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.970
It's heavy stuff that the movie doesn't always
deploy gracefully, making for bracing moments

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.500
that get way too real.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.340
Be alright

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:43.190
The movie ends in fire as the showdown in
the Park Hill projects comes to a violent,

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:44.280
C-4-fueled conclusion.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:48.830
The end of the fight just happens to coincide
with the end of the 12-hour experiment period.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:52.080
Just like that, the island is returned to
a state of relative calm.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:57.580
After the shootout, Dmitri, Nya, Isaiah and
Dolores join the crowd outside in the light

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:01.160
of dawn, reconnecting with the community after
the night of violence.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:05.760
Instead of tearing each other apart as the
NFFA intended, the citizens defended each

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.360
other - a moral victory, if nothing else.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:12.820
As the movie ends, the Purge is over - now,
to paraphrase the movie's final words, it's

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.000
time to fight.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:19.300
The movie's hopeful ending stands in contrast
to what we know about where the story is going.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:23.220
The residents of Staten Island don't succeed
in stopping the Purge from spreading nationwide,

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:27.160
and the tradition doesn't end for years, or
potentially decades.

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:32.620
Despite this, the movie concludes to the hopeful
strains of Kendrick Lamar's "Alright", a modern-day

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:36.800
anthem of resolve and resilience that's used
now to represent resistance.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:41.080
No matter how many Purges happen in the future,
people will always try to help each other

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:41.820
and survive.

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:43.740
People will always fight back.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.820
In a series this bleak, that's a victory in
itself.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:48.740
Thanks for watching!

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.350
